From a2c75112cecabc037a4f50855ee6a06d76ac4d6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neha Virani <NehaVirani@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:52:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Isolate evaluation data by user account

Each saved answer and test run now records its owner (rag_responses.user_id,
evaluation_runs.user_id), and every evaluation endpoint enforces ownership in
the backend:

- evaluations.php lists, dashboards, metric summaries and comparisons only
  include the signed-in user's rows; response details and human reviews return
  404 for another user's answer
- evaluate_standalone.php, run_evaluation.php and exports.php return 404 for
  another user's answer or run
- test_runs.php records the new run's owner and only accepts the user's own
  baseline
- Migration 011 assigns owners where provable (conversation owner, run owner)
  without deleting anything; rag/claim_evaluations.py assigns pre-account
  history to one account
- Two-account HTTP tests cover listing, opening, reviewing, scoring,
  comparing and exporting, plus the migration and claim command

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015X6GjaC31WebNrBymNFZ4N
